\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 \uc0\u9989  How to Enter the aicamp Environment\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Open Terminal.\
Then:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 \
cd ~\
source aicamp/bin/activate\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf0 If you created it in your home directory (
\f2\fs26 ~
\f1\fs24 ), this works.\
If you created it inside another folder (for example 
\f2\fs26 ~/projects
\f1\fs24 ), then:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 \
cd ~/projects\
source aicamp/bin/activate\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 \uc0\u55357 \u56590  How You Know It\'92s Active\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Your terminal will change to something like:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 \
(aicamp) lingjiamacbook@MacBook-Air-von-Lingjia ~ %\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf0 That 
\f2\fs26 (aicamp)
\f1\fs24  in front means:\uc0\u8232 \u55357 \u56393  You are inside Python 3.12 virtual environment.\
Check version to be sure:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 \
python --version\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf0 It should show:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 \
Python 3.12.x\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 \uc0\u55357 \u57002  How to Leave the Environment\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 When you\'92re done:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 \
deactivate\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf0 That returns you to your normal system Python.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 \uc0\u55357 \u56481  Pro Tip (So You Don\'92t Panic Tomorrow)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 If you\'92re unsure where 
\f2\fs26 aicamp
\f1\fs24  lives, run:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 \
find ~ -name aicamp -type d\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf0 It will show the exact path.\
